WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.138
<v DANA>Let's talk about sharps containers that
are almost full. I'll be honest, if a bin

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:09.120
<v DANA>looks like it has room, I just use it
without checking the top.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.180
<v RAY>[thoughtful] Well, that's the tricky
thing. A container can be at its fill

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:17.517
<v RAY>line and still have a gap at the top.
From where you're standing, it looks like

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.240
<v RAY>there's room.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.400
<v DANA>So how would I know it's full?

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.473
<v RAY>Look for the fill line, not the GAP. Once
the sharps reach that line, it's full.

00:00:25.473 --> 00:00:29.840
<v RAY>Pushing another one in puts your hand
close to what's already inside.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.160
<v DANA>So the container can fool you. Does that
happen anywhere else?

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.022
<v RAY>Actually, it can happen with a regular
trash bin too. Imagine you walk past one,

00:00:39.022 --> 00:00:43.760
<v RAY>and something's half-hidden under paper
towels, and you can't tell what it is.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.928
<v DANA>So you've got a container with a gap at
the top and something in a bin you can't

00:00:48.928 --> 00:00:51.120
<v DANA>identify. Which one's the hazard?

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.861
<v RAY>BOTH of them could be. A sharp that's
hidden in other material or mixed into

00:00:55.861 --> 00:00:58.560
<v RAY>regular trash puts the next person at
risk.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.880
<v DANA>[skeptical] Even if you're not sure it's
a sharp?

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:05.309
<v RAY>[matter-of-fact] Yes, even then. Spotting
a hazard early prevents injuries, even

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:07.440
<v RAY>when you can't be sure what it is yet.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.880
<v DANA>So the hazard counts before you even know
what it is.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.905
<v RAY>That's it. And for the container, the
rule is simple: at the fill line, it's

00:01:15.905 --> 00:01:16.240
<v RAY>full.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.720
<v DANA>[sighs] Honestly, if it looked roomy, I
figured it was fine.

